Complete the tutorial’s basic workflow and advanced sections, then read the writing-rules, configuration, distribution/reproducibility, caching, monitoring, and provenance material relevant to a project. Compare its graph and execution semantics with Make. One substantial workflow tool can support the practical project; reading a second helps distinguish the underlying method from a particular syntax.

The official tutorial describes automatic dependency graphs and resource-constrained execution, including distributed settings and environment integration. Record the exact implementation version, configuration, and selected execution method for a run. Preserve project documentation/software notices; the example data remain at their authorized external locations. Official tutorial and available topics checked on 29 October 2026.

